          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Pierre\",\"addressee\":\"Hélène\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Je vous aime!\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.98,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. Its conventional and hesitant delivery may bear on sincerity or spontaneity, but it remains an explicit avowal of a loving state.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Теперь уж поздно, всё кончено; да и я люблю ее», подумал Пьер.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.79,\"reason\":\"In this occurrence, the avowal also moderately affirms Pierre's acceptance of the marital bond already being publicly imposed and treated as settled. He says the socially required words while holding the hand of the woman identified as his fiancée, so the expression ratifies his position as her prospective husband. It is not itself a separately worded proposal or detailed promise; Prince Vasily's blessing is a separate speech act that supplies context rather than substituting for Pierre's undertaking.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях», думал он\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime! — сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"The words are not represented as a reflexive affective outburst. Pierre pauses, recalls the expected formula, and deliberately says it; the exclamation mark does not override that depiction.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях; но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"No additional core force is needed beyond avowal and contextual ratification of the engagement. The expression's socially scripted quality modifies those functions rather than establishing a distinct residual mode.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях», думал он, но никак не мог вспомнить, чтó такое именно говорят в этих случаях.\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Pierre and Hélène have been left alone after Prince Vasily has publicly treated them as engaged and blessed their anticipated marriage. Following Hélène's kiss, Pierre searches for the conventional words expected on such an occasion and tells her that he loves her, with an embarrassed and inadequate-sounding delivery.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal avowal moderately ratifies Pierre's socially established role as Hélène's fiancé and implicitly affirms the prospective marital bond. The commitment's terms are not articulated within the expression, and the father's prior blessing is a separate act. Hélène gives no verbal acceptance after the focal words in the supplied passage, though the preceding kiss, their treatment as an engaged couple, and the subsequently reported marriage provide contextual uptake.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passage is recognisable as Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly represents Pierre as attracted to Hélène and internally thinking that he loves her, but it also emphasizes pressure, fear, shame, and formulaic compliance. Those features complicate sincerity and voluntariness without removing the utterance's avowal or its moderate engagement-ratifying force.\"}"
